# Reproducible Release Candidate

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M4 Candidate packaging
Dependencies: 08_LOCAL_STORAGE.todo, 09_HOTKEYS_RECOVERY.todo, 10_PRESENTATION_MODE.todo, 11_DPI_ACCESSIBILITY.todo, 12_DIAGNOSTICS_TESTING.todo, 19_LIVE_TRANSCRIPTION.todo, 21_BACKGROUND_TRANSLUCENCY.todo, 22_NATIVE_PYTHON_RUNTIME.todo, 24_CURSOR_AND_FOCUS.todo, 25_TRANSCRIPT_FIRST_THEMES.todo, 26_MICROPHONE_AND_COMPUTER.todo, 39_INSTALLED_CLI_ANSWERS.todo, 32_ANSWER_UI_LIFECYCLE.todo, 34_ANSWER_PRIVACY_RESILIENCE.todo

## Purpose

Produce the exact installable/runnable candidate that final qualification will test.

## Tasks

- [ ] Approve self-contained versus framework-dependent distribution and supported architectures.
- [ ] Pin runtime patch, dependency locks, release version, source identity, and reproducible build recipe.
- [ ] Publish the proposed x64 ZIP without assuming single-file/trimming/AOT is appropriate for WPF.
- [ ] Include approved license/notices, checksums, release notes, privacy/support boundaries, and data policy.
- [ ] Exclude notes, recovery, context stores, private captures, credentials, dumps, and development tooling.
- [ ] Smoke-test a clean supported Windows account/machine without developer SDK or elevation.
- [ ] Test first launch, no-taskbar recovery, relocation, upgrade/rollback data handling, exit, and removal.
- [ ] Resolve signing identity/key custody if distribution requires it; never store keys in the repo.
- [ ] Record unsigned/signed status, SmartScreen/enterprise-policy behavior, and runtime patching ownership.
- [ ] Freeze the candidate hash for workstream 13; rebuilds invalidate that candidate's qualification.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Artifact launches on the declared clean-machine baseline and contains exactly intended files.
- [ ] Runtime dependencies/patch responsibilities are clear; no unsupported binary trick is required.
- [ ] Package identity/hash and contents are reproducible and recorded.
- [ ] Signing/reputation/enterprise policy are described without guaranteed warning-free installation.
- [ ] This task creates a candidate only; it does not imply capture qualification or public release.

